# C# / .NET Conventions

## Target

- `net10.0`, nullable enabled, file-scoped namespaces
- Follow `.editorconfig` and StyleCop (enforced at build)
- XML documentation on all public APIs (`GenerateDocumentationFile` is enabled)

## Dependencies

- Central Package Management: add versions in `Directory.Packages.props` only
- Never pin package versions in individual `.csproj` files
- Shared test deps: `build/dependencies.props`

## Code style

- Explicit access modifiers; `sealed` when inheritance is not intended
- Composition over inheritance; avoid unnecessary abstraction layers
- Prefer modern C# when it improves clarity

## Public API

- Strongly typed, discoverable, predictable
- No magic strings, ambiguous booleans, or hidden side effects
- Breaking changes require explicit justification (NuGet consumers)
